---
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout title="Contribute" description="Help shape Varve through reproducible bug reports, product discussions, testing, documentation, design feedback, and future code contributions.">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="contribute-page">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Contribute to Varve</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">
        Varve is community-shaped. Clear bug reports, thoughtful workflow ideas, cross-platform testing, documentation, and design feedback all help the project move forward.
      </p>
      <p class="page-hero-sub" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
        <strong>Contributions are open for docs and examples, translations, plugins in your own repository, testing and device reports, and the nine libraries under MIT OR Apache-2.0.</strong> App code remains maintainer-only for now. See <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a> for details.
      </p>

      <section class="contribute-section">
        <h2>Ways to Help Today</h2>
        
        <div class="contribute-cards site-card-grid">
          <div class="contribute-card site-card site-card--surface">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <div class="cc-icon cc-icon-teal" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Bug Reports</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Give the maintainer a reliable reproduction</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Search existing <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/issues">Issues</a> first</li>
              <li>Include steps, expected and actual result, and environment</li>
              <li>Add screenshots, logs, or a small source document when useful</li>
              <li>Use <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/issues/new?template=bug_report.yml">the bug template</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="contribute-card site-card site-card--surface">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <div class="cc-icon cc-icon-sand" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8Z"/><path d="M14 2v6h6"/><path d="M16 13H8"/><path d="M16 17H8"/><path d="M10 9H8"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Documentation &amp; Examples</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Make the product easier to understand and use</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Point out confusing or stale passages</li>
              <li>Share tutorials, examples, and workflow recipes</li>
              <li>Suggest screenshots or accessibility improvements</li>
              <li>Use the <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/issues">docs issue form</a> for corrections and <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/discussions">Discussions</a> for examples</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="contribute-card site-card site-card--surface">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <div class="cc-icon cc-icon-terra" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.5 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7.5L14.5 2z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><path d="m9 15 2 2 4-4"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Cross-Platform Testing</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Expand confidence beyond the maintainer's machine</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Record OS, architecture, package type, and Varve version</li>
              <li>Test on Linux, macOS, and Windows where available</li>
              <li>Check keyboard access and screen-reader behavior</li>
              <li>Confirm fixes and report regressions with exact actions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="contribute-card site-card site-card--surface">
            <div class="cc-head">
              <div class="cc-icon cc-icon-ink" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 19l7-7 3 3-7 7-3-3z"/><path d="m18 13-1.5-7.5L2 2l3.5 14.5L13 18l5-5z"/><path d="m2 2 7.586 7.586"/><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="2"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Workflow &amp; Design Feedback</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Help prioritize the next useful design-tool improvement</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Describe the task you are trying to complete</li>
              <li>Share a sketch, mockup, or before/after comparison</li>
              <li>Discuss interaction, accessibility, and visual hierarchy</li>
              <li>Post proposals in <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/discussions">Discussions</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="contribute-section">
        <h2>Contribution lanes</h2>
        <p>
          Docs and examples, translations, plugins in your own repository, testing and device reports, and contributions to the nine MIT OR Apache-2.0 libraries are open today. App code remains maintainer-only for now.
        </p>
        <p>
          Start with <code>pnpm verify:plan</code>, run <code>pnpm verify:affected</code>, and record the commands in the pull request. The full gate is reserved for explicit high-impact changes and requires a stated reason. See the <a href={sitePath('/contribute/guidelines')}>contribution guidelines</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/docs/development/contributing.md">development contributor guide</a> for the complete workflow.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="contribute-section">
        <h2>Getting Started Today</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Read the <a href={sitePath('/contribute/guidelines')}>contribution guidelines</a> and <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md">code of conduct</a></li>
          <li>Search existing Issues and Discussions before starting a new thread</li>
          <li>Choose Issues for reproducible bugs and Discussions for ideas, workflows, and architecture</li>
          <li>Include platform, version, exact steps, and evidence that helps someone reproduce the report</li>
          <li>For local development, follow <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/docs/development/setup.md">the setup guide</a> and <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/AGENTS.md">AGENTS.md</a></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="contribute-section">
        <h2>Contribution Licensing</h2>
        <p>
          The app is source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT. Contributions use DCO 1.1 sign-off under the licence of the files changed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contributors are credited in release notes. See <a href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md">CONTRIBUTING.md</a> for the DCO text and PR process.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="contribute-section">
        <h2>Recognition</h2>
        <p>
          Contributors are recognized in the following ways:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>GitHub contributor list (automatic)</li>
          <li>Release notes acknowledgment (with permission)</li>
          <li>Contributors section on the About page</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="contribute-cta">
        <h2>Get involved</h2>
        <Button href="https://github.com/varvedesign/varve/discussions">Follow GitHub Discussions</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .contribute-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  
  .contribute-page .page-hero-title {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .contribute-page .page-hero-sub {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .contribute-page .page-hero-sub:last-of-type {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  
  .contribute-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  
  .contribute-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .contribute-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .contribute-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(300px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .contribute-card {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  .contribute-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  /* Icon + title as a flex row: icon cannot overlap the title at any
     zoom level, and the layout stays stable when titles wrap. */
  .cc-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cc-head .cc-icon {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  .cc-head h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Icon + title sit side by side in a flex row, in normal flow, so the
     icon can never overlap the title at any font size, zoom, or reflow. */
  .cc-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .cc-icon {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--website-radius-control);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .cc-icon-teal {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-teal) 12%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-teal);
  }

  .cc-icon-sand {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-sandstone) 12%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-sandstone);
  }

  .cc-icon-terra {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-terracotta) 12%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-terracotta);
  }

  .cc-icon-ink {
    background: var(--surface-muted);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .contribute-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  
  .contribute-card p {
    font-size: var(--type-interface-control-size);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .contribute-card ul {
    list-style: none;
  }
  
  .contribute-card li {
    font-size: var(--type-interface-readout-size);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  
  .contribute-card li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-link-hover);
  }
  
  .contribute-section ol {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: item;
  }
  
  .contribute-section ol li {
    counter-increment: item;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 2.5rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  
  .contribute-section ol li::before {
    content: counter(item);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--status-built);
    color: var(--text-on-status);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: var(--type-interface-micro-size);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  
  .contribute-section ul {
    list-style: none;
  }
  
  .contribute-section li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  
  .contribute-section li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-link-hover);
  }
  
  .contribute-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  
  .contribute-cta h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
</style>
